# Dest / main promote

Applies to every `livo-tv` repo that has `dev` (not `harness`).

## Do

- Land product work (features, fixes, lockfiles, library pins) on **`dev`**
- Reach `main` only by promoting dest (`dev` → `main` **merge commit**, never squash)
- After `release.yml` on `main` (or a hotfix on `main`), merge **`main` back into dest**
  - Fast-forward dest when dest has nothing new
  - Otherwise a merge commit
  - Wait for dest CI
- Treat dest-behind (`chore(release): X.Y.Z` only on `main`) as a blocker for the next dest → `main` PR

Runbook: `harness/platform/promote-dev-to-main.md` (`/promote`). ADR 0026.

## Do not

- Skip dest ← `main` after a stable cut because dest "already has the product work" — the release commit is new history on `main`. The next dest → `main` PR will conflict on `package.json` / CHANGELOG
- Re-promote a dest-sync-only merge (that fold is not a second product path)
- Open the same product change on dest and `main` in parallel
- Promote dest while it is behind `main`
- Force-push `main` or dest
